 "notes": "Spine: gap -> DTE ligand design -> complexation -> coordination structure -> photo-isomerisation -> Eu and Yb emission quenching (two parallel branches) -> PDMS films -> encryption. Figures opened: F2, F4, F6, F9. F1/F3/F5/F10 not opened; nodes relying on them are text_only with fig_ref_unopened. F7, F8 carry no caption. Notable multimodal act: t13 reads Eu emission (F4) against closed-DTE absorption (F2) on the same wavelength axis across two figures (overlap), and the absence of overlap for Yb forces a second quenching route. Audits: t24 (5ooo fatigue cycles reach <half PSS absorbance), t30 (method limit on emission spectra). t22 photograph shows a written 'UR1' code the text does not describe; the emission-level (NIR) encryption itself is not demonstrated, so t29 basis=argued. t7 -> t11 by supports: the crystal structure of the closed form (5ccc) indirectly confirms both the complex and that DTE closes in it.",
 "migrated_from": "r04/graphs/Advanced_Functional_Materials__10.1002_adfm.202002943.json"
}